<title>USA: LCRA 550 MW Texas coal unit seen up in nine weeks.</title>
<headline>LCRA 550 MW Texas coal unit seen up in nine weeks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lower Colorado River Authority (LCRA) said Tuesday its 550 megawatt Fayette coal-fired power unit 3 was expected to be out of service for about nine weeks for scheduled maintenance.</p>
<p>The unit, located just east of La Grange, Texas, was taken off line over the weekend for the scheduled work, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Fayette unit 3 is fully owned by LCRA.</p>
<p>Fayette units 1 and 2, both also rated at 550 megawatts, are equally owned by LCRA and the city of Austin.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
